Kubernetes Security Checklist Table
| # | Phase / Activity | Component / Tool | Best Practice / Security Goal | Implementation Detail / Config | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Static Code Analysis | Gitleaks | Scan full Git history for hardcoded secrets, Prevent credential leaks | Regex & Entropy scanning via GitHub Actions | Critical |
| 2 | Static Code Analysis | Kube-linter | Validate Kubernetes manifests against security rules, Enforce configuration standards | Ensure runAsNonRoot and resource limits | High |
| 3 | Static Code Analysis | Hadolint | Lint Dockerfiles for optimization and security, Minimize image vulnerabilities | Avoid using latest tags and root users | Medium |
| 4 | Secure Container Build | Docker Buildx | Compile multi-stage container images, Reduce attack surface | Separate build environment from final runtime | High |
| 5 | Secure Container Build | Base Images | Use Alpine or Distroless as base layers, Eliminate unnecessary OS utilities | Remove tools like curl, apt, and bash from prod | High |
| 6 | Image Vulnerability Scan | Trivy | Scan OS packages and application dependencies, Detect known CVEs before deployment | Fail pipeline if CRITICAL or HIGH CVEs found | Critical |
| 7 | Artifact Registry | GHCR / Docker Hub | Push verified container images to private registry, Ensure image provenance | Use Least Privilege permissions (packages:write) | Medium |
| 8 | Cluster Admission Control | Kyverno / OPA | Enforce policies inside the cluster at runtime, Block manual unsecure deployments | Reject non-compliant YAMLs at API Server level | High |
| 9 | Runtime Application | Pod Lifecycle | Configure Graceful Shutdown preStop hooks, Maintain zero-downtime rolling updates | Add sleep 15 to allow network propagation | High |
